<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaragoza</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaragoza is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro River</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> the capital of an important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. It was the most important Almoravid city in north-eastern Spain. Its fall to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> in 1118 marked the deterioration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>' northern front.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaragoza.jpg" alt="Zaragoza" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Turol Jones, un artista de cojones from Villanueva del Cascajal, República Independiente de Mi Casa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zaragoza_-_Bas%C3%ADlica_del_Pilar_y_r%C3%ADo_Ebro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
